# The portable triple's lit configuration (plan 5.18.10 PX1-PX3, P-1a.i):
# nested runs of lit.cfg.py on the synthetic suite Inputs/nested-portable,
# whose one test prints the portable substitutions and, one line each, the
# features that tell a portable run from a host-triple run. Every nested run
# with the portable triple passes msil_probe_cache= (empty), so its probes,
# some of which fail where the portable toolchain is missing, neither read
# nor replace the outer run's probe cache. Checks:
# (1) --param msil_triple=msil64-unknown-dotnet: %msil_portable_triple,
# %clang_portable, %llc_portable, %{msil_portable_cflags} (-nolibc
# -ffreestanding), %msil_dotnet_x86 (msil-run.py --expect-os windows with
# the limits and the x86 dotnet), %msil_set_32bitreq and %clang_native's
# stand-in for a triple without a native one; the features
# msil-triple=msil64-unknown-dotnet, msil-triple-portable and
# msil-triple-msil64 and none of a host triple (msil-triple-windows,
# msil-triple-linux), the native oracle or the hosted programs; and the
# derived features msil-portable, msil-portable-builtins and msil-dotnet-x86
# exactly when the outer run has them (the same probes). %msil_exec expects
# the host OS's files, or linux under msil_runner=wsl (5.17.4's portable
# allowance).
# (2) The configuration errors, each fatal (exit 2) with its text: the -msil
# suffix on the portable triple, x86_64-unknown-dotnet, msil_native_oracle=
# required, and msil_require_portable and msil_require_x86 other than 0 or 1;
# msil_native_oracle=1 is a warning and the run goes on.
# (3) msil_require_portable=1 loads exactly when the outer run has
# msil-portable, msil-portable-builtins and msil-portable-sysroot (P-1b's
# sysroot), and otherwise is fatal naming what is missing;
# msil_require_x86=1 loads exactly when the outer run has msil-dotnet-x86,
# and is fatal under msil_runner=wsl on Windows.
# (4) A host-triple run of msil/test/Portable (the outer run's triple when it
# is not the portable one) reports every test UNSUPPORTED (P-1a.l's
# lit.local.cfg) and runs none.
# The patterns write cl[a]ng and l[l]c, which lit's tool substitutions
# leave alone. Each check pins its failure path: (2) and the fatal branches of (3) are
# the failures of (1) and of the loading branches.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t

# (1)
# RUN: %{harness_lit} -a --param msil_triple=msil64-unknown-dotnet --param msil_probe_cache= %S/Inputs/nested-portable > %t/1.log 2>&1
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/1.log "^PASS: MSIL :: harness/portable/Inputs/nested-portable/flags\.test " "^# \| portable triple: \[msil64-unknown-dotnet\]$" "^# \| cl[a]ng portable: \[\S*cl[a]ng(\.exe)? --target=msil64-unknown-dotnet\]$" "^# \| l[l]c portable: \[\S*l[l]c(\.exe)? -mtriple=msil64-unknown-dotnet\]$" "^# \| portable cflags: \[-nolibc -ffreestanding\]$" "^# \| cl[a]ng native: \[\S*cl[a]ng(\.exe)? --target=no-native-triple-of-msil64-unknown-dotnet\]$" "^# \| set 32bitreq: \[.*msil-run\.py --set-32bitreq\]$" "^# \| dotnet x86: \[.*msil-run\.py --expect-os windows --timeout \d+ --mem-limit-mb \d+ --dotnet .+\]$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/1.log "^# \| feature msil-triple=msil64-unknown-dotnet$" "^# \| feature msil-triple-portable$" "^# \| feature msil-triple-msil64$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} lacks %t/1.log "^# \| feature msil-triple-windows$" "^# \| feature msil-triple-linux$" "^# \| feature msil-native-oracle$" "^# \| feature msil-hosted$"
# RUN: %if msil-portable %{ %{harness_check} contains %t/1.log "^# \| feature msil-portable$" %}
# RUN: %if !msil-portable %{ %{harness_check} lacks %t/1.log "^# \| feature msil-portable$" %}
# RUN: %if msil-portable-builtins %{ %{harness_check} contains %t/1.log "^# \| feature msil-portable-builtins$" %}
# RUN: %if !msil-portable-builtins %{ %{harness_check} lacks %t/1.log "^# \| feature msil-portable-builtins$" %}
# RUN: %if msil-dotnet-x86 %{ %{harness_check} contains %t/1.log "^# \| feature msil-dotnet-x86$" "^# \| dotnet x86: \[.* --dotnet (?!dotnet-x86-not-found\])\S.*\]$" %}
# RUN: %if !msil-dotnet-x86 %{ %{harness_check} lacks %t/1.log "^# \| feature msil-dotnet-x86$" %}
# RUN: %if msil-wsl %{ %{harness_check} contains %t/1.log "^# \| exec: \[.*msil-run\.py --expect-os linux " %}
# RUN: %if !msil-wsl && system-windows %{ %{harness_check} contains %t/1.log "^# \| exec: \[.*msil-run\.py --expect-os windows " %}
# RUN: %if !msil-wsl && !system-windows %{ %{harness_check} contains %t/1.log "^# \| exec: \[.*msil-run\.py --expect-os linux " %}

